# Code owners for AgriCarbon Atlas.
#
# Why this file exists: carbon parameters, policy rules, the privacy boundary and the
# supply chain are the parts of the repository that people act on or that can leak data,
# so GOVERNANCE.md requires a domain reviewer for them. Branch protection enforces it
# once "Require review from Code Owners" is switched on (infra/github/README.md).
#
# The team handles below are PLACEHOLDERS. GitHub reports an owner that does not exist
# as an error and ignores the line, so this file does nothing until you either create
# these teams in the agricarbon-atlas organization or point every line at real handles.
# A single-maintainer project can name one handle on every line and still benefit from
# the explicit mapping.
#
#   @agricarbon-atlas/maintainers        everything not listed below, supply chain, licensing
#   @agricarbon-atlas/carbon-reviewers   parameters, equations, tree-age rules
#   @agricarbon-atlas/policy-india       IN program rules and notes
#   @agricarbon-atlas/policy-usa         US program rules and notes
#   @agricarbon-atlas/policy-eu          EU program rules and notes
#   @agricarbon-atlas/privacy-reviewers  geometry handling, logging, explain, agents, schema
#
# Rules: the LAST matching pattern wins, so keep general patterns first.
# Area labels for the same paths come from .github/labeler.yml.

# Default owner for everything
*                                       @agricarbon-atlas/maintainers

# Numbers people act on: require a carbon domain reviewer
/config/species/                        @agricarbon-atlas/carbon-reviewers
